**Read:** Complete the assigned Simon, Tong, Cambridge and IFUSP progression, the available MIT electronic/optical work, and Ralph's seven sections. Revisit the existing electromagnetic and thermal material where a derivation depends on it.

Develop all three linked studies. They can share a material platform or use different examples; each must connect composition and processing, structure, a model, an observable and its limitations. Use complete primary methods and evidence, not an abstract as a substitute for the reported experiment.

Include a derivation, an independently checked calculation, a competing explanation and a prediction under a changed condition. Where data or equipment are unavailable, provide a reproducible model investigation and a specific experimental proposal, clearly distinguished from performed work. Follow the branches in any useful order, then bring their results to the review.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
